name:           podman-test
version:        0.1.0
synopsis:       Podman containers for tests, in parallel, reached through Unix sockets
description:    Run the services that a test needs, such as a database or a node, in
                rootless Podman containers, from any test framework. Every run of the
                tests has its own containers and its own folder of Unix sockets, so test
                processes run in parallel without sharing ports. A service that listens
                on a Unix socket is reached directly; one that only listens on TCP is
                bridged to a socket; TCP ports on the loopback interface are there when
                a client needs them. Containers that a dead run left behind are removed
                by the next one.
category:       Testing
stability:      experimental
homepage:       https://github.com/jprupp/podman-test#readme
bug-reports:    https://github.com/jprupp/podman-test/issues
author:         JP Rupp
maintainer:     jprupp@protonmail.ch
